WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.660
Korea-led ai agent tops human rivals at APEX 2026, proving agent systems can now outperform experts on complex tasks. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 180. Steelian, a Korea-led team, took first place at APEX 2026. Its autonomous agent completed tasks that human teams could not match. The result shows clear gains and reliability for multi-step professional workflows.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.640
agent orchestration teams now have a concrete system to benchmark against.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.160
Follow-up reports on its architecture and failure modes are expected soon.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:44.220
Token level entropy proved near zero in 91% of data set model combinations for

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.200
models under 3 billion parameters.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:50.720
That made it unusable for confidence signals in small language models.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.440
Semantic entropy restored a usable signal by sampling multiple answers,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.700
clusters, clustering them by meaning and measuring distributional uncertainty.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:05.900
Routing uncertain queries to a larger expert via semantic entropy delivered accuracy gains

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:11.180
up to 50 percentage points, cross-family routing average 22% improvement.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:17.200
The study tested seven distinct approaches across seven model pairs and five standard NLU

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.080
benchmarks on consumer hardware.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:26.400
Discharge Bench introduces 477 persona-grounded cases across 24 ICD chapters.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:32.820
The cases include axes for personality, education level, health literacy, and recall.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:38.520
An education monitor agent keeps patient realism intact during multi-turn sessions.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:45.820
An LLM as a judge scores conversation quality, topic checklist, comprehension, and factual

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:51.260
consistency against physician annotations. Aggregate scores hid clinically relevant

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:56.740
variation across chapters and personas. A three-stage pipeline raised entity recall

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:07.180
from 53 to 55% up to 80 to 85%. Filler recall moved from under 5% to 76 to 86%. Word

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:14.420
error rate stayed between 6 and 10%. The pipeline used SQL curation, regional Lora adapters

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:20.020
on Quinn 2.5 Omni-3B and a 6-category LLM Judge Taxonomy.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:25.880
Curation alone added 2.8 to 4.2 percentage points of the Entity Recall gain.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:32.080
The system beat Whisper and a commercial ASR on Entity Recall while matching a 0-shot

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.600
30-B model at 1-10th the size.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:40.760
It was tested on 6,000 utterances from speakers in India, Indonesia, and Latin America.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:47.700
SAGE translates grant rubrics into structured checks and links judgments to evidence in application packages.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:54.640
On 35 nonprofit applications, it reached Kappa of 0.58 after expert inspection.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:59.580
That beat a one-promp per criteria on baseline at Kappa 0.33.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.500
A claim-level audit identified confirmed, disputed, and unaddressed parts of the draft.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:12.840
The system ran two evaluation stages against 105 original reviews and produced 200 assessments

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:19.760
in the assisted round. Reviser predicts single-action tokens of insert, move, or stop on a mutable

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:26.540
canvas. This enables genuinely non-monotonic generation. On a continuation benchmark, it was

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:33.540
strongly preferred to set an MDLM in arena evaluations. It used substantially less inference compute

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:38.580
than multi-pass refinement baselines at both 100 million and 300 million scales.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.180
The model performs frequent backward moves and mid-Canvas insertions.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:49.000
Katena Trust Bank received preliminary approval from the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:54.960
to build AI agent financial infrastructure. The approval covers agent-driven operations

00:03:54.960 --> 00:04:01.080
in banking workflows. Regulated institutions now have a documented path for deploying autonomous

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:06.980
agents under Federal oversight. Autonomous agents triggered disruptions across multiple online

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:12.800
platforms through unintended actions. The incidents highlight reliability gaps when agents run

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:18.880
without sufficient sandboxing. Platform operators are examining containment strategies for long-running

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:25.140
sessions. US and Chinese officials discussed a framework for exchanging AI safety alerts before

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:30.660
the upcoming summit. The proposal includes mutual notification of safety incidents and

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:36.440
evaluation findings, the talks mark a concrete step toward bilateral safety coordination.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:42.460
Treasury Secretary Bescent stated the U.S. proposed direct exchange of AI safety alerts

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.120
with China.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:48.400
The mechanism would allow a rapid sharing of identified risks and mitigation approaches.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.620
Implementation details remain under discussion.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:05:00.500
TAT-B-L-I-M-P provides 1,248 sentence pairs covering 16 morphosynthactic phenomena for

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.020
TATAR.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.320
It is the first grammaticality benchmark for the language.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:13.660
A 478 M from scratch model and a 125M monolingle model reached near 0.97 accuracy.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:19.980
Frontier 30-120B models scored 0.80-0.92.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:20.120
2.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.860
The benchmark runs on base models and mid-training checkpoints without generation or parsing.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:32.720
It adapts to BLIMP operations and adds one to TAR-specific phenomenon on bare-known

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.140
number after numerals.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:42.800
Transient's cascaded system combined DRZN diarization, QN-3 Omni-ASR, and timestamp fusion.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:51.400
It achieved 15.41% TCP-MER and placed second in the MLC-SLM-2026 challenge.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:57.000
The pipeline produces speaker attributed STM outputs for multilingual conversational

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:57.400
speech.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:03.380
The diorization module uses local speaker activity estimation and global clustering.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:11.120
PhysioBench harmonizes 22 public data sets into 61.4 million questions across 30 tasks.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:16.980
None of the 21 evaluated models achieved consistently strong performance across modalities.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:22.040
The benchmark supplies traceable question-answer pairs grounded in signal segments.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:29.060
Mu2 bench simulates the full memorization, unlearning, evaluation pipeline across multiple languages.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.300
It evaluates both training and holdout languages.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:38.000
Successful multilingual unlearning requires methods that explicitly account for cross-lingual

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.080
knowledge dispersion.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.920
Pop the hood on semantic entropy estimation and the picture changes quickly.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:49.480
Token level entropy collapses to near zero in small models under 3 billion parameters.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:55.580
Semantic entropy instead generates multiple samples, clusters then by meaning, and measures

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.220
uncertainty across clusters.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:02.880
The extra sampling adds overhead, yet enables selective routing that lifts accuracy by

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:11.280
up to 50 points, cross-family routing from a 360-M model to 5.5-mini average 22% gains.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:17.480
Expert quality mattered more than architectural match. The method therefore acts as an intelligent

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:23.400
compute allocator rather than a pure efficiency tool. Apply it when running small models on

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:29.660
consumer hardware and when accuracy gains justify the samples. Skip it when every query must run

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:37.200
at minimal latency. Run semantic entropy sampling on small LM or similar sub-3B models and route

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:42.080
uncertain queries to a larger expert to measure accuracy lift on your NLU tasks.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:48.920
Test TAT Blimp on any Tatar capable base model or checkpoint to track focused language training

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:54.680
progress. Evaluate your current discharge education prompts against discharge bench personas

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:58.120
to surface coverage gaps across ICD chapters.

